<h5>

Our Guru

</h5>

<h2>

Guru Bhagavathi Kulkarni

</h2>

<div class="small-divider">

<span></span>

<i class="fa-solid fa-dharmachakra"></i>

<span></span>

</div>

<p>

Guru Bhagavathi Kulkarni began learning Bharatanatyam at the young age of
<strong>6 years</strong> under the guidance of
<strong>Karnataka Kalashree Awardee Guru Smt. Jyothi Pattabhiram.</strong>

</p>

<p>

She successfully completed her
<strong>Junior Dance Examination</strong>
while studying in the
<strong>5th Standard</strong>,
demonstrating her dedication and passion for Bharatanatyam from an early age.

</p>

<p>

Later, she continued her Bharatanatyam training under
<strong>Guru Anant Chinchansur</strong>
in Raichur, where she underwent intensive training for
<strong>three years</strong>,
strengthening her technical knowledge and artistic expression.

</p>

<p>

After a gap of
<strong>10 years</strong>,
her love and devotion for Bharatanatyam inspired her to resume learning under
<strong>Vidushi Smt. Maitreyee B.</strong>

</p>

<p>

She successfully completed her
<strong>Senior Dance Examination</strong>
and continues learning Bharatanatyam even today, believing that classical dance is a lifelong journey of learning, discipline and self-improvement.

</p>

<p>

Through
<strong>Radhashankari Dance Academy</strong>,
Guru Bhagavathi Kulkarni is committed to preserving the rich heritage of Bharatanatyam while inspiring students with confidence, discipline, cultural values and artistic excellence.

</p>

